# route: level=w4_l1_coop difficulty=expert players=2 ends=exit after=tally expect=eggs:0,wipes:0,x2_gates:2,painting:27,min_checkpoints:3
# The Expert two-stream route of Cinder Shaft in co-op (designer DB3; P1|P2, keys L R U D F K S; recorded from
# closed-loop duo macros, build/db3/bot_w4_l1_coop.gd). The view sinks one pixel per tick: P1 plays the solo club
# route's keys where the co-op map is the solo map and P2 follows his trail 24 ticks behind (a ledge apart on the
# zigzags, never under or over him); both hop the Shellback of the first gallery, push the heave boulder left into
# the chute together (gate 'boulder': it plugs the vent of the lava pool below), drop onto it one after the other
# as the pool comes into view and hop to the right bank; in the Cinder Cache P2 Shoulder-Hops off P1's head onto
# the shelf for Cave Painting 27; through the ember chute, the spike strata, the cavern and the Ember Hoard to the
# magma chamber, where P2 Shoulder-Hops onto the 8-row cliff (gate 'cliff'), clubs the coiled vine down and P1
# climbs it; both walk into the exit (the team exit). Some hurts, no egg. Nobody stands 243 ticks without input.
